      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "High expression of vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) induces subepithelial fibrosis associated with angiogenesis in patients with asthma. Thrombin is recognized as a new candidate mediating airway remodeling. Therefore, this study was designed to determine the role of up-regulated thrombin activity induced by VEGF on airway remodeling in patients with asthma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Levels of biochemical parameters in induced sputum were examined in 21 asthmatic patients and 11 normal control subjects."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Thrombin activity in induced sputum was significantly higher in asthmatic patients than in normal control subjects: median, 3.67 U/mL; range, 1.15 to 10.2 U/mL; vs median, 1.26 U/mL; range, 0.93 to 2.42 U/mL (p < 0.0001). In contrast, protein C activity in induced sputum was lower in asthmatic patients than in normal control subjects: median, 20%; range, 5 to 30%; vs 41%; range, 30 to 59% (p < 0.0001). VEGF level in induced sputum was positively correlated with thrombin activity in asthmatic patients (r = 0.55, p = 0.02), while inversely correlated with protein C activity (r = - 0.57, p = 0.01). Levels of basic fibroblast growth factor (bFGF), a major profibrotic factor, were also significantly higher in asthmatic patients than in normal control subjects. Moreover, thrombin activity was significantly correlated with bFGF level in asthmatic patients (r = 0.67, p = 0.003)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Increase in VEGF level leads to up-regulation of thrombin activity in asthmatic airways, and this elevated thrombin activity induces elevation of bFGF level. It will become to be a new strategy of asthma therapy to attenuate thrombin activity for the regulation of airway remodeling."
        }
      ]},
